Docker Image -> contains all the facilities needed to run an app like runtime, src code, dependencies and config needed in SpringBoot Project
It gives a real production like environment for deploying application like redis , load balancer , cross proxy server etc it containerize them so that there is no version mismatch during runtime.
Docker Image Repository this is were all the docker images are stored.
Once a image is pulled into Docker Image Repository the containers are created and this were the application runs.
Set up the environments variables and the bind ports for accessing the db through host port because we cannot access from container port.
And then Bind Mounts for backup data , since once the container is restarted the data in the app will be lost so it is used as a backup. The containers run independently in separate environments to we are adding it to a network so it can communicate with each other.
