Architecture Explanation
Frontend → communicates with Patient Service using REST (JSON).
Patient Service → calls Billing Service using gRPC.
Appointment Service → also calls Billing Service using gRPC.
gRPC communication uses Protocol Buffers defined in:
billing_service.proto
Billing Service exposes a gRPC Server.
Other microservices act as gRPC Clients.

In gRPC(microservices using it)
use gRPC and proto dependencies in pom.xml
The build section in pom has some build steps to build the Protocol Buffer file whenever we restart the app, it tells the maven to do it.
The maven helps in generating the code to interact with the billing Service grpc server(The code is generated in the target folder)
A gRPC stub is a generated client class that allows one service to call remote gRPC methods like normal Java methods.
